    "text": "def sort_numbers(numbers: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\" Input is a space-separated, numerically sorted string of numerals from  'zero' to 'nine'. Valid choices are 'zero', 'one', 'two', 'three', 'four', 'five', 'six', 'seven', 'eight', 'nine'. Return the string with numbers sorted from smallest to largest.\n    >>> sort_numbers('three one five')\n    'one three five'\n    \"\"\"\n    num_list = numbers.split()\n    sorted_numbers = sorted(num_list, key=lambda x: int(x))\n    return sorted_numbers\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    import doctest\n    doctest.testmod()\n```",
